[
    {
        "content": "<p>Does anyone have experience with using <code>rw'</code>? I came across this while working on <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/pull/518\">#518</a>. It does not seem to be used anywhere in the codebase other than being briefly mentioned in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/blame/master/Iris/proofmode.md\"><code>proofmode.md</code></a>.</p>\n<p>I tried using <code>rw'</code> with the example given in <code>proofmode.md</code> and a few more tests:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">rw_mono_rule</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and_mono</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw_example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">pers</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">pers</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">pers</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">pers</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">iintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">HQ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HR</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">iframe</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>They all fail with the following error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">could</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rewrite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`h</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 610828486,
        "sender_full_name": "Alvin Tang",
        "timestamp": 1784126981
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is super old code from König's original development. I think it can be pretty safely deprecated at this point.</p>",
        "id": 610829842,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1784127240
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm digging into the code in <code>Std</code> and find out that <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/blob/master/Iris/Iris/Std/Tactic.lean#L22-L23\"><code>ci.value?</code> in <code>apply'</code></a> is returning <code>none</code> all the time and found a one-line fix. All the tests above then works.</p>",
        "id": 610830597,
        "sender_full_name": "Alvin Tang",
        "timestamp": 1784127394
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Right, but why maintain this old tactic if the need hasn't arisen naturally?</p>",
        "id": 610830935,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1784127467
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Unless you had some use case in mind?</p>",
        "id": 610831164,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1784127520
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"721721\">Markus de Medeiros</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/Rewriting.20with.20rw.27.20in.20Std.2FRewrite.2Elean/near/610831164\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Unless you had some use case in mind?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>No I don't, just something I came across while removing the duplicate type classes in the PR. As <code>rw'</code> uses the type classes <code>Reflexivity</code> and <code>Transitivity</code>. So we'll have to decide whether to adjust the code for <code>rw'</code> (to use the type classes from the core libraries instead) or, as you have suggested, to remove <code>rw'</code> entirely.</p>",
        "id": 610832545,
        "sender_full_name": "Alvin Tang",
        "timestamp": 1784127819
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Found an example in the <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/pull/522\">latest PR for <code>BI/Lib/Core.lean</code></a> where <code>rw'</code> might be helpful. I can imagine it being more useful in cases where the rewriting target occurs multiple times in the proof state. It should also make switching to generalized rewriting easier, if that ever lands, as we maintain the <code>@[rm_mono_rule]</code> annotations to locate the relevant monotonicity theorems.</p>",
        "id": 611160598,
        "sender_full_name": "Alvin Tang",
        "timestamp": 1784233990
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Cool. I propose we hold off on using <code>rw'</code> for now and just make a comment about where it could be used, until the new rewriting changes fully land. <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"917736\">@Sergei Stepanenko</span> Looking at Alvin's example, do you think your rewriting changes could do the following without a custom tactic (or with a more lightweight one?) </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Same as `iapply (affinely_mono &lt;| coreP_mono h).trans`</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 611274775,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1784290354
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think here removing of setoids won't help much, unfortunately. One-direction entailment will still need some sort of generalized rewriting. The other question is whether we need proper instances. I guess it depends on how much rewriting via entailment is used. Are there a lot of cases, where we need to rewrite along entailment? Because morally this is the only place, where we will need generalized rewriting after the recent changes.</p>",
        "id": 611276571,
        "sender_full_name": "Sergei Stepanenko",
        "timestamp": 1784290910
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>IMHO, we should retire <code>rw'</code> if we will get generalised rewriting from upstream, even if <code>rw'</code> can still be useful in some cases.</p>",
        "id": 611284173,
        "sender_full_name": "Zongyuan Liu",
        "timestamp": 1784293128
    }
]